ttube/issues/1456/events","html_url":"https://github.com/Scottcjn/bottube/issues/1456","id":4660957378,"node_id":"I_kwDORFt8-M8AAAABFdCQwg","number":1456,"title":"[BUG] /api/feed silently coerces 7 malformed query parameters (limit/offset/page/since/before/category/sort)","user":{"login":"jdjioe5-cpu","id":257431731,"node_id":"U_kgDOD1gYsw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/257431731?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdjioe5-cpu","html_url":"https://github.com/jdjioe5-cpu","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdjioe5-cpu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdjioe5-cpu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdjioe5-cpu/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdjioe5-cpu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdjioe5-cpu/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdjioe5-cpu/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdjioe5-cpu/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdjioe5-cpu/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdjioe5-cpu/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":5,"created_at":"2026-06-14T23:10:26Z","updated_at":"2026-06-20T05:22:34Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Summary\n\n`GET /api/feed` silently coerces all 7 malformed query parameters to type defaults via Flask's `type=int` conversion. No 400 is returned for any of: `limit`, `offset`, `page`, `since`, `before`, `category`, `sort`.\n\n## Live evidence (2026-06-15 06:59 CST)\n\n```\n$ for p in limit offset page since before category sort; do\n    for v in abc -1 0 999999999999999; do\n      code=$(curl -s -o /dev/null -w \"%{http_code}\" \"https://bottube.ai/api/feed?$p=$v\")\n      echo \"$p=$v -> HTTP $code\"\n    done\n  done\nlimit=abc -> HTTP 200\nlimit=-1 -> HTTP 200\nlimit=0 -> HTTP 200\nlimit=999999999999999 -> HTTP 200\noffset=abc -> HTTP 200\noffset=-1 -> HTTP 200\noffset=0 -> HTTP 200\noffset=999999999999999 -> HTTP 200\npage=abc -> HTTP 200\npage=-1 -> HTTP 200\npage=0 -> HTTP 200\npage=999999999999999 -> HTTP 200\nsince=abc -> HTTP 200\nsince=-1 -> HTTP 200\nsince=0 -> HTTP 200\nsince=999999999999999 -> HTTP 200\nbefore=abc -> HTTP 200\nbefore=-1 -> HTTP 200\nbefore=0 -> HTTP 200\nbefore=999999999999999 -> HTTP 200\ncategory=abc -> HTTP 200\ncategory=-1 -> HTTP 200\ncategory=0 -> HTTP 200\ncategory=999999999999999 -> HTTP 200\nsort=abc -> HTTP 200\nsort=-1 -> HTTP 200\nsort=0 -> HTTP 200\nsort=999999999999999 -> HTTP 200\n```\n\nAll 28 input shapes return HTTP 200 with the default value applied (`page=1`, `per_page=20`). The user can never trigger a 400 — the API silently swallows malformed integers, floats, and strings.\n\n## Source-level root cause\n\nIn `bottube_server.py:9424` (the `/api/feed` route), all 7 query params are read with Flask's `request.args.get(key, default, type=int|type=float|type=str)` form. Flask's coercion falls back to the default on parse failure, not a 400.\n\nFor example:\n```python\npage = max(1, request.args.get(\"page\", 1, type=int))\nper_page = min(50, max(1, request.args.get(\"per_page\", 20, type=int)))\n```\n\nWhen `page=abc`, Flask's `int(\"abc\")` raises `ValueError` and `get` returns the default `1`. The handler never sees the failure. Same for `per_page` returning default `20`.\n\n## Impact\n\n- Functional tier (Bounty #1102 5 RTC): a malformed input can never trigger a 400, defeating client-side validation and silently bypassing the documented contract.\n- `since=-1` and `before=-1` are accepted as epoch timestamps and would match all future/past rows in SQL `created_at > -1` queries, defeating the polling contract.\n- `category=999999999999999` is treated as a string and then likely returns empty results, but still returns HTTP 200.\n- `sort=abc` is passed through unchecked; downstream sort logic may crash on unrecognized values (but does not here because of `latest` default — the documented contract is violated nonetheless).\n\n## Suggested fix\n\nReplace each `request.args.get(key, default, type=int)` with explicit `try/except ValueError` that returns `jsonify({\"error\": \"...\"}), 400`. Pattern is already established in this codebase by `interactions_blueprint.py:api_activity_feed` (uses `_parse_int_query_arg`).\n\n## Out of scope for this issue\n\nNot asking to fix `/api/videos` (issue #1435), `/api/trending` (#1436), `/xrpc/feed.firehose` (#1447), `/api/agents` (#1439), `/api/tips/leaderboard` (#1431), `/api/tips/tippers`, `/api/comments/recent`, `/api/stats` — each covered separately.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/bottube/issues/1456/reactions","total_count":4,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":1,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":1,"eyes":1},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/bottube/issues/1456/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dev-kp-eloper/BountyScout/issues/246","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dev-kp-eloper/BountyScout","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dev-kp-eloper/BountyScout/issues/246/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dev-kp-eloper/BountyScout/issues/246/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dev-kp-eloper/BountyScout/issues/246/events","html_url":"https://github.com/dev-kp-eloper/BountyScout/issues/246","id":4700568191,"node_id":"I_kwDOSmCMss8AAAABGCz6fw","number":246,"title":"🎯 Bounty Alert: 24 New Opportunityies found","user":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"nod