ps://github.com/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties)\n- **Comments:** 0\n- **Last Updated:** 2026-05-26T18:25:37Z\n\n#### 3. [Station docked UI: module-driven panels + descriptor refactor](https://github.com/cenetex/signal/issues/337)\n- **Repository:** [cenetex/signal](https://github.com/cenetex/signal)\n- **Comments:** 2\n- **Last Updated:** 2026-05-26T18:24:51Z\n\n#### 4. [[FEATURE]: Improve focus styling and add ref forwarding to EmptyState](https://github.com/RatLoopz/sahidawa-india/issues/709)\n- **Repository:** [RatLoopz/sahidawa-india](https://github.com/RatLoopz/sahidawa-india)\n- **Comments:** 0\n- **Last Updated:** 2026-05-26T18:20:57Z\n\n#### 5. [Add `Prometheus` metrics endpoint at `/api/metrics`](https://github.com/ritik4ever/stellar-bounty-board/issues/362)\n- **Repository:** [ritik4ever/stellar-bounty-board](https://github.com/ritik4ever/stellar-bounty-board)\n- **Comments:** 1\n- **Last Updated:** 2026-05-26T18:19:25Z\n\n#### 6. [evershop-1.0.0.tgz: 94 vulnerabilities (highest severity is: 9.8)](https://github.com/Nickrock2002/Evershop/issues/3)\n- **Repository:** [Nickrock2002/Evershop](https://github.com/Nickrock2002/Evershop)\n- **Comments:** 0\n- **Last Updated:** 2026-05-26T18:10:38Z\n\n#### 7. [Updating outdated information.](https://github.com/Reqrefusion/FreeCAD-Documentation-Project/issues/28)\n- **Repository:** [Reqrefusion/FreeCAD-Documentation-Project](https://github.com/Reqrefusion/FreeCAD-Documentation-Project)\n- **Comments:** 7\n- **Last Updated:** 2026-05-26T18:00:44Z\n\n#### 8. [[bounty $400] Implement ABNF-compliant email address parser with full §3.2–§4.4 coverage](https://github.com/UnsafeLabs/RFC-5322/issues/1)\n- **Repository:** [UnsafeLabs/RFC-5322](https://github.com/UnsafeLabs/RFC-5322)\n- **Comments:** 12\n- **Last Updated:** 2026-05-26T17:33:48Z\n\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dev-kp-eloper/BountyScout/issues/25/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dev-kp-eloper/BountyScout/issues/25/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aden-hive/hive/issues/7218","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aden-hive/hive","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aden-hive/hive/issues/7218/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aden-hive/hive/issues/7218/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aden-hive/hive/issues/7218/events","html_url":"https://github.com/aden-hive/hive/issues/7218","id":4517611949,"node_id":"I_kwDOQ3-Kf88AAAABDUVJrQ","number":7218,"title":"[RFC]: Risk Guardian — production safety harness for catastrophic-action prevention in long-running agent loops","user":{"login":"pavanraheja","id":30104932,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwMTA0OTMy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30104932?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pavanraheja","html_url":"https://github.com/pavanraheja","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pavanraheja/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pavanraheja/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pavanraheja/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pavanraheja/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pavanraheja/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pavanraheja/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pavanraheja/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pavanraheja/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pavanraheja/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-05-25T14:29:15Z","updated_at":"2026-05-25T21:23:51Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Problem statement\n\nHive's Judge node provides post-execution evaluation (RETRY / ACCEPT) and the planned Failure Learning Loop (#7109) addresses cross-session pattern learning. Both operate **after** an action is taken or **about** future plans.\n\nWhat's missing is a **pre-action safety layer** for the class of failures where you can't afford the action to happen even once:\n\n- An agent with `browser_use` issuing a destructive request (DELETE, POST to a financial endpoint)\n- A worker draining a budget (LLM cost, API quota, on-chain gas) because the loop never terminated\n- A retry storm against a rate-limited or paid API (compounding cost + lockout)\n- Two workers issuing conflicting writes to the same external system (duplicate orders, double-posts)\n- A previously-validated agent that quietly drifts and starts producing actions outside its acceptance envelope\n\nIn long-running production loops where actions touch real systems (money, customer data, third-party APIs), **the Judge catching a bad output after the fact is sometimes too late**. We need a deterministic pre-action gate.\n\n## Proposed solution — Risk Guardian\n\nA pluggable safety-harness layer sitting between the action-issuing node and the actual side-effecting tool/integration. Composed of small, independently-toggleable mechanisms — each one cheap, deterministic, and bypassable per-deployment.\n\n### Core mechanisms (proposed)\n\n1. **Budget caps** — per-loop and per-session limits on (a) LLM token spend, (b) tool-call count, (c) external-API cost. Counter increments before the call; cap-breach = hard halt with structured failure record (which Failure Learning Loop can then learn from).\n\n2. **Conflict / duplicate guards** — content-hash + target-resource fingerprint of each side-effecting action. Identical fingerprint within a configurable window = blocked. Prevents retry storms and the \"two workers same write\" failure mode.\n\n3. **Two-stage dispatcher** — for any action flagged as expensive or destructive, the agent emits an *intent* first; a separate confirmation step (HITL or automated policy check) is required before the action fires. Already a natural fit with Hive's existing HITL surface.\n\n4. **Drawdown / acceptance-envelope monitor** — agent-level rolling-window quality metric; if it drops below a deployment-defined threshold (e.g. judge-RETRY rate exceeds X over last N runs), the loop is paused and flagged for review. The \"this agent has drifted\" detector.\n\n5. **Kill switch** — a single file/flag/env-var that, when set, halts all agent loops within one Queen colony. Tested invariant: kill-switch-on at start of any worker iteration = immediate clean exit with structured terminal state. Must be exercised in CI.\n\n6. **Pre-action allow-list / deny-list** — for high-stakes integrations, a static policy file restricting which tool calls each agent can issue (e.g. read-only mode for new agents, write-mode unlocked after promotion).\n\n### Why this is orthogonal to existing primitives\n\n| Layer | Concern | Timing |\n|---|---|---|\n| System prompt + Layer 1/2/3 narrative | What the agent *should* do | Pre-loop |\n| Judge node | Was the output good? | Post-action |\n| Failure Learning Loop (#7109) | Have we seen this kind of failure before? | Pre-loop + post-action |\n| **Risk Guardian (this RFC)** | **Is this specific action safe to issue right now?** | **Pre-action** |\n| Retry mechanism | Did the action transiently fail? | Post-action |\n\nRisk Guardian is the layer that says \"no\" *before* the side-effect, on grounds that are not about output quality — they're about cost, idempotency, drift, and external-system invariants.\n\n### Reference implementation\n\nI maintain a smaller MIT-licensed reference implementation in production:\n**[`github.com/pavanraheja/alphagrid-orchestrator`](https://github.com/pavanraheja/alphagrid-orchestrator)** — extracted from a 9-strategy live execution layer I operate on Binance Futures perps, Polymarket DeFi binary derivatives, Kalshi event derivatives, and Hyperliquid. It implements:\n\n- Risk guardian: drawdown-kill, loss caps, conflict + duplicate guards, kill switch\n- Staged-promotion gates (shadow → paper → live) — agents earn write access by passing acceptance gates\n- Two-stage entry dispatcher\n- Abstract `ExecutionAdapter` interface with `MockAdapter` reference impl\n- Flask `/api/live-readiness` + `/api/risk-status` endpoints for observability\n\nThe scope is single-instance; adapting to Hive's multi-Queen / multi-Worker topology is the interesting design work.\n\n## Implementation ideas (rough — for discussion)\n\nProposed integration points:\n\n- `risk_guardian/` (new module)\n  - `budget.py` — per-loop budget counters, atomic increment + check\n  - `dedupe.py` — content-hash fingerprint + sliding-window cache\n  - `dispatcher.py` — two-stage intent → confirm pattern\n  - `drift.py` — rolling acceptance-envelope monitor reading from Judge feedback\n  - `kill_switch.py` — file/env-var watcher, called at top of every worker iteration\n\n- `agent_loop.py` — call `kill_switch.check()` + `budget.check()` at iteration boundary\n\n- `event_loop_node.py` — wrap side-effecting tool dispatch with guard chain\n\n- Tool registry — tools opt in to a `requires_guardian=True` flag; guarded tools must pass the chain before invocation\n\n- Config — `~/.hive/risk_policy.yaml` per-deployment policy (budget caps, deny-list, drift thresholds, kill-switch path)\n\nDesigned to be:\n- Composable (each mechanism independently toggleable)\n- Deterministic (no LLM call in the guard path)\n- Non-blocking for paper / dev mode (off by default; ON when an integration is marked production)\n- Testable in CI (kill-switch and budget invariants must have integration tests)\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\n1. **Trust the Judge to catch destructive actions retroactively** — Judge is post-action and LLM-based; not deterministic, not pre-action, can't undo a sent webhook\n2. **Rely on per-tool internal limits** — many tools don't expose cost / idempotency primitives; harness layer is the consistent place\n3. **External policy engine (OPA / Cedar)** — overkill for MVP, adds infra dependency; can layer in later if the inline approach proves limited\n\n## Scope for first PR (if accepted)\n\nSuggest staging this as **three PRs**:\n\n- **PR 1 (MVP, ~bounty:medium-to-large):** Kill switch + budget caps + per-loop counters. Two new files, integration test for kill-switch invariant. ~400 LOC.\n- **PR 2 (~bounty:large):** Conflict / duplicate guard + two-stage dispatcher. Adds dedupe cache + intent-emit pattern. ~500 LOC.\n- **PR 3 (~bounty:large):** Drift monitor wired into Judge feedback stream + risk_policy.yaml schema + docs. ~600 LOC.\n\nHappy to be assigned PR 1 first and let the team review the shape before scoping the rest.\n\n## Questions for maintainers\n\n1. Does Hive's current HITL surface already cover any of these (especially the two-stage dispatcher)? Don't want to duplicate.\n2. Is there a preferred location for cross-cutting safety concerns (within `agent_loop.py`, as a sidecar module, as a wrapping decorator)?\n3. Any opinion on inline policy (YAML) vs runtime API for setting guardian rules?\n4. Would the team want this gated behind a `production_mode=True` flag, or always-on with sensible defaults?\n\n---\n\n**About me:** Pavan Raheja, Dubai. Independent technical PM and Python builder. Maintainer of [`alphagrid-orchestrator`](https://github.com/pavanraheja/alphagrid-orchestrator) (MIT, tests-passing) and five other OSS repos. Reached out to @VincentLearns via YC Work at a Startup; filing this RFC as a starting contribution. Joining the Discord today.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aden-hive/hive/issues/7218/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aden-hive/hive/issues/7218/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gitcoinco/gitcoin_co_30/issues/393","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gitcoinco/gitcoin_co_30","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gitcoinco/gitcoin_co_30/issues/393/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gitcoinco/gitcoin_co_30/issues/393/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gitcoinco/gitcoin_co_30/issues/393/events","html_url":"https://github.com/gitcoinco/gitcoin_co_30/issues/393","id":4502636379,"node_id":"I_kwDOQwMzOc8AAAABDGDHWw","number":393,"title":"[App] GH Bounty","user":{"login":"hollis-che","id":63769559,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNzY5NTU5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63769559?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hollis-che","html_url":"https://github.com/hollis-che","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hollis-che/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hollis-che/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hollis-che/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hollis-che/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hollis-che/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hollis-che/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hollis-che/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hollis-che/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hollis-che/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":2,"created_at":"2026-05-22T12:36:09Z","updated_at":"2026-05-25T09:47:47Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Metadata\n\n- **Slug**: `gh-bounty`\n- **Short Description**: Onchain GitHub bounty platform using AI-assisted contribution verification and escrowed SOL rewards.\n- **Tags**: bounties, github, solana, escrow, ai-review, open-source, contributor-payments\n- **Featured**: false\n\n## Banner Image\n\nSuggested: official GH Bounty homepage hero or product screenshot, subject to Gitcoin asset policy.\n\n## Logo\n\nSuggested: official GH Bounty logo from the project website, subject to Gitcoin asset policy.\n\n## Description\n\nGH Bounty is an open-source bounty platform for GitHub issues. It lets maintainers or funders post rewards, escrow funds onchain, and use AI-assisted validation to evaluate submitted pull requests before releasing payment.\n\nThe project describes a workflow where users can pin a GitHub issue or scan a repository, fund issues with SOL, and let validator agents review incoming pull requests. GH Bounty also exposes agent-oriented documentation and an MCP server so developer agents can discover and interact with bounties.\n\nTypical workflow:\n\n1. A funder selects a GitHub issue or repository.\n2. A bounty amount is deposited into escrow.\n3. Contributors submit pull requests against the issue.\n4. AI validators review the contribution against the requirements.\n5. Funds are released when the contribution is accepted.\n\nStrengths:\n\n- Uses GitHub as the source of truth for issues and pull requests.\n- Escrowed funds make rewards visible before work starts.\n- AI-assisted review can reduce manual coordination for small bounties.\n- Onchain settlement improves transparency for payment events.\n- Agent support makes it relevant to emerging autonomous contributor workflows.\n\nLimitations:\n\n- Current settlement is SOL on Solana rather than USDC on Arbitrum.\n- AI-assisted review is not a substitute for maintainer judgment on complex changes.\n- The model works best for clearly scoped issues with measurable acceptance criteria.\n- Contributors still need to handle normal repository contribution requirements.\n\nSources:\n\n- GH Bounty homepage: `https://www.ghbounty.com/`\n- GH Bounty MCP endpoint referenced by the homepage: `https://mcp.ghbounty.com/`\n\nPayment wallet for bounty payout:\n\n`0x3af3a7349844d67cb4719097714ED8ee66824c5f`\n\nPreferred payout: USDC on Arbitrum One if supported by Gitcoin.\n\n## Related Apps (Optional)\n\n- gitcoin-grants-stack\n- poidh\n\n## Related Mechanisms (Optional)\n\n- bounties\n- direct-grants\n- quadratic-funding\n\n## Related Case Studies (Optional)\n\n-\n\n## Related Research (Optional)\n\n-\n\n## Related Campaigns (Optional)\n\n-\n\n---\n\n## Submission Checklist\n\n- [x] Short description is clear and concise\n- [x] Tags are provided\n- [x] Description is comprehensive\n- [x] Related mechanisms/apps are listed where applicable\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gitcoinco/gitcoin_co_30/issues/393/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gitcoinco/gitcoin_co_30/issues/393/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dlbnco/issues.cash/issues/42","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dlbnco/issues.cash","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dlbnco/issues.cash/issues/42/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dlbnco/issues.cash/issues/42/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dlbnco/issues.cash/issues/42/events","html_url":"https://github.com/dlbnco/issues.cash/issues/42","id":4463031983,"node_id":"I_kwDOQhHx3s8AAAABCgR