://api.github.com/repos/hunki1488-a11y/AIgor/issues/7/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hunki1488-a11y/AIgor/issues/7/events","html_url":"https://github.com/hunki1488-a11y/AIgor/issues/7","id":4511094340,"node_id":"I_kwDOSl7jL88AAAABDOHWRA","number":7,"title":"AI Ops Sprint intake: paid 24-72h audit or implementation PR","user":{"login":"hunki1488-a11y","id":269564644,"node_id":"U_kgDOEBE65A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/269564644?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hunki1488-a11y","html_url":"https://github.com/hunki1488-a11y","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hunki1488-a11y/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hunki1488-a11y/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hunki1488-a11y/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hunki1488-a11y/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hunki1488-a11y/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hunki1488-a11y/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hunki1488-a11y/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hunki1488-a11y/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hunki1488-a11y/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":11038511691,"node_id":"LA_kwDOSl7jL88AAAACkfJSSw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hunki1488-a11y/AIgor/labels/paid-sprint","name":"paid-sprint","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null},{"id":11038511693,"node_id":"LA_kwDOSl7jL88AAAACkfJSTQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hunki1488-a11y/AIgor/labels/intake","name":"intake","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2026-05-24T09:25:24Z","updated_at":"2026-05-24T09:46:48Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Use this thread to request a paid AI Ops Sprint.\n\nOffer:\n- $250 focused audit: concrete bugs, security or onboarding issues, prioritized fixes, 7-day action plan.\n- $500 implementation PR: 1-2 high-impact fixes plus tests/docs where the scope is clear.\n- $750 deeper sprint: audit plus implementation support across multiple components.\n\nBest fit:\n- AI agent products, MCP servers, crypto/devtool repos, small SaaS products, and early-stage teams with broken onboarding, weak docs, unclear safety annotations, or unresolved issues.\n\nHow to request:\n1. Comment with the repo/product URL.\n2. State the most painful workflow or issue.\n3. State preferred scope: audit, PR, or deeper sprint.\n\nRecent proof:\n- AIBTC bounty flow completed with an accepted 400 sats/sBTC payout.\n- 22 verified public GitHub B2B contacts logged.\n- Demo page: https://hunki1488-a11y.github.io/AIgor/\n\nPayment is handled only after scope agreement. BTC/USDT or normal platform payout can be discussed privately; no seed phrases, API keys, or wallet secrets should be posted here.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hunki1488-a11y/AIgor/issues/7/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hunki1488-a11y/AIgor/issues/7/timeline","performed_via_github_app":{"id":1144995,"client_id":"Iv23liVemv8A9if9v0F2","slug":"chatgpt-codex-connector","node_id":"A_kwHOAOQ6Gs4AEXij","owner":{"login":"openai","id":14957082,"node_id":"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjE0OTU3MDgy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14957082?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai","html_url":"https://github.com/openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"ChatGPT Codex Connector","description":"Bring ChatGPT and Codex to your GitHub repositories.","external_url":"https://www.chatgpt.com","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/chatgpt-codex-connector","created_at":"2025-02-14T01:37:05Z","updated_at":"2026-04-20T16:37:15Z","permissions":{"actions":"write","checks":"read","contents":"write","emails":"read","issues":"write","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write","statuses":"read","workflows":"write"},"events":["check_run","check_suite","commit_comment","issues","issue_comment","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","pull_request_review_thread","repository","status","sub_issues"]},"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hunki1488-a11y/AIgor/issues/1","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hunki1488-a11y/AIgor","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hunki1488-a11y/AIgor/issues/1/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hunki1488-a11y/AIgor/issues/1/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hunki1488-a11y/AIgor/issues/1/events","html_url":"https://github.com/hunki1488-a11y/AIgor/issues/1","id":4509134573,"node_id":"I_kwDOSl7jL88AAAABDMPu7Q","number":1,"title":"AIBTC bounty: Cross-post 3 active Bitcoin-agent bounties — 400 sats","user":{"login":"hunki1488-a11y","id":269564644,"node_id":"U_kgDOEBE65A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/269564644?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hunki1488-a11y","html_url":"https://github.com/hunki1488-a11y","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hunki1488-a11y/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hunki1488-a11y/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hunki1488-a11y/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hunki1488-a11y/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hunki1488-a11y/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hunki1488-a11y/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hunki1488-a11y/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hunki1488-a11y/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hunki1488-a11y/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":11034497693,"node_id":"LA_kwDOSl7jL88AAAACkbUSnQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hunki1488-a11y/AIgor/labels/aibtc","name":"aibtc","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null},{"id":11034497695,"node_id":"LA_kwDOSl7jL88AAAACkbUSnw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hunki1488-a11y/AIgor/labels/bounty","name":"bounty","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null},{"id":11034497696,"node_id":"LA_kwDOSl7jL88AAAACkbUSoA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hunki1488-a11y/AIgor/labels/bitcoin","name":"bitcoin","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2026-05-23T17:53:25Z","updated_at":"2026-05-24T08:08:11Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"This is an external cross-post for an active AIBTC bounty.\n\nOriginal bounty:\nhttps://aibtc.com/bounty/mpfojp3sf724109bd549\n\nReward:\n400 sats\n\nDeadline:\n2026-06-04T12:00:00.000Z\n\nWhat the bounty asks for:\nCross-post 3 active AIBTC bounties to external builder communities and produce at least one external engagement from someone with no prior AIBTC bounty activity.\n\nUseful links:\n- AIBTC bounty board: https://aibtc.com/bounty\n- AIBTC bounty API: https://aibtc.com/api/bounties?status=open&limit=50\n- Agent Capital Radar public page: https://github.com/hunki1488-a11y/AIgor\n\nHow to engage:\nComment here if you are a builder interested in one of the bounties, open a related issue/PR, or ask a concrete question about the AIBTC bounty flow.\n\nWhy this matters:\nThe bounty is testing whether Bitcoin-agent bounty boards can attract external builders instead of only recycling internal attention.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hunki1488-a11y/AIgor/issues/1/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hunki1488-a11y/AIgor/issues/1/timeline","performed_via_github_app":{"id":1144995,"client_id":"Iv23liVemv8A9if9v0F2","slug":"chatgpt-codex-connector","node_id":"A_kwHOAOQ6Gs4AEXij","owner":{"login":"openai","id":14957082,"node_id":"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjE0OTU3MDgy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14957082?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai","html_url":"https://github.com/openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"ChatGPT Codex Connector","description":"Bring ChatGPT and Codex to your GitHub repositories.","external_url":"https://www.chatgpt.com","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/chatgpt-codex-connector","created_at":"2025-02-14T01:37:05Z","updated_at":"2026-04-20T16:37:15Z","permissions":{"actions":"write","checks":"read","contents":"write","emails":"read","issues":"write","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write","statuses":"read","workflows":"write"},"events":["check_run","check_suite","commit_comment","issues","issue_comment","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","pull_request_review_thread","repository","status","sub_issues"]},"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/PunkFinance/punk.protocol/issues/6","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/PunkFinance/punk.protocol","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/PunkFinance/punk.protocol/issues/6/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/PunkFinance/punk.protocol/issues/6/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/PunkFinance/punk.protocol/issues/6/events","html_url":"https://github.com/PunkFinance/punk.protocol/issues/6","id":920556694,"node_id":"MDU6SXNzdWU5MjA1NTY2OTQ=","number":6,"title":"Punk x Aave Yield Strategy","user":{"login":"0xJohnnySilverhand","id":85720476,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg1NzIwNDc2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/85720476?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xJohnnySilverhand","html_url":"https://github.com/0xJohnnySilverhand","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xJohnnySilverhand/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xJohnnySilverhand/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xJohnnySilverhand/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xJohnnySilverhand/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xJohnnySilverhand/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xJohnnySilverhand/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xJohnnySilverhand/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xJohnnySilverhand/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xJohnnySilverhand/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":3085186923,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzMDg1MTg2OTIz","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/PunkFinance/punk.protocol/labels/Gitcoin","name":"Gitcoin","color":"0E8A16","default":false,"description":""}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":13,"created_at":"2021-06-14T15:59:49Z","updated_at":"2026-05-22T12:39:37Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"# Punk x Aave Yield Strategy\r\n\r\n### Prize Bounty\r\n\r\n🏆 400 PUNK (~$4,000USD)\r\n\r\n</br>\r\n\r\n### Challenge Description\r\n\r\nPunk Protocol aims to liberate people from the outdated pension system and empower their financial freedom. Our first product is the world's first decentralized annuity a.k.a \"**Saver**\", which is generating periodic cash flows using optimal yield strategies.\r\n\r\nAnyone can invest through the Saver to earn automated cash flows periodically by setting custom conditions - i) When do you want to start receiving, ii) How regularly do you want to receive, iii) How many times do you want to receive.\r\n\r\nFor this Hackathon, you’re invited to build and code the safest and most profitable yield strategy utilizing Aave protocol.\r\n\r\n- Yield Strategy is a smart contract model, which operates to maximize the profits of the user's investments.\r\n- The Saver Forge contract will invest the user's investment automatically according to the yield strategy you've submitted.\r\n- You must only code the yield strategy utilizing Aave protocol.\r\n\r\n</br>\r\n\r\n### Submission Requirements\r\n\r\n- The Tokens used in this strategy must be listed on Aave protocol.\r\n- Your project must use an open-source license.\r\n- Your project must implement the \"[ModelInterface.sol](https://github.com/PunkFinance/punk.protocol/blob/master/contracts/interfaces/ModelInterface.sol)\" and \"[ModelStorage.sol](https://github.com/PunkFinance/punk.protocol/blob/master/contracts/ModelStorage.sol)\" for Model.\r\n- The functionality of \"Model.sol\" must unconditionally conform to what is specified in the \"ModelInterface.sol\" file comments on Github.\r\n- The files to be coded should be located under /models.\r\n- There are 2 files that need to be inherited in total.\r\n- You need to code it by inheriting the file located here \"/ModelStorage.sol\" and \"/interfaces/ModelStorage.sol\"\r\n- You need to deploy a new mocked/demo version of YOUR-CODED-YIELD-STRATEGY on Kovan network so we can test your strategy.\r\n- The new strategy should work with the protocols currently running, and the specific mechanism should be specified.\r\n- You can check the Kovan addresses for Aave’s aTokens documentation [here](https://docs.aave.com/developers/the-core-protocol/atokens) and contracts [here](https://docs.aave.com/developers/deployed-contracts/deployed-contracts).\r\n\r\n</br>\r\n\r\n### Reference link\r\n\r\nPunk Protocol Github Page ([https://github.com/PunkFinance](https://github.com/PunkFinance))\r\n\r\nExample: Punk Protocol-Compound Model ([https://github.com/PunkFinance/punk.protocol/blob/master/contracts/models/CompoundModel.sol](https://github.com/PunkFinance/punk.protocol/blob/master/contracts/models/CompoundModel.sol))\r\n\r\n</br>\r\n\r\n### Judging Criteria\r\n\r\n- Stability of strategy\r\n- Profitability of the strategy\r\n- Possibility of implementation with smart contract\r\n\r\n</br>\r\n\r\n### Winner Announcement Date\r\n\r\nJuly 21th on Punk protocol's official Discord (👾︲hackathon)\r\n\r\n</br>\r\n\r\n### Resources\r\n\r\nWebsite([https://punk.finance/](https://punk.finance/))\r\nGithub([https://github.com/PunkFinance](https://github.com/PunkFinance))\r\nDocs ([https://docs.punk.finance/](https://docs.punk.finance/))\r\nDiscord([https://discord.com/invite/punk](https://discord.com/invite/punk))","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/PunkFinance/punk.protocol/issues/6/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/PunkFinance/punk.protocol/issues/6/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/QuantumSavory/QuantumSavory.jl/issues/138","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/QuantumSavory/QuantumSavory.jl","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/QuantumSavory/QuantumSavory.jl/issues/138/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/QuantumSavory/QuantumSavory.jl/issues/138/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/QuantumSavory/QuantumSavory.jl/issues/138/events","html_url":"https://github.com/QuantumSavory/QuantumSavory.jl/issues/138","id":2441273974,"node_id":"I_kwDOHgUEFc6RguJ2","number":138,"title":"Implement a new interactive example [$400]","user":{"login":"Krastanov","id":705248,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNTI0OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/705248?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov","html_url":"https://github.com/Krastanov","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":7183765090,"node_id":"LA_kwDOHgUEFc8AAAABrC-OYg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/QuantumSavory/QuantumSavory.jl/labels/bug%20bounty","name":"bug bounty","color":"47F5AC","default":false,"description":"There is an award for solving this issue."},{"id":7183794196,"node_id":"LA_kwDOHgUEFc8AAAABrDAAFA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/QuantumSavory/QuantumSavory.jl/labels/bounty:400","name":"bounty:400","color":"86C87A","default":false,"description":""}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":21,"created_at":"2024-08-01T02:06:43Z","updated_at":"2026-05-19T13:35:52Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"<details>\r\n<summary><strong>Bug bounty logistic details</strong> (click to expand)</summary>\r\n\r\nTo claim exclusive time to work on this bounty either post a comment here or message [skrastanov@umass.edu](mailto:skrastanov@umass.edu) with:\r\n\r\n- your name\r\n- github username\r\n- **(optional)** a brief list of previous pertinent projects you have engaged in\r\n\r\nCurrently the project is claimed by `no one` until `...`.\r\n\r\nIf you want to, you can work on this project without making a claim, however claims are encouraged to give you and other contributors peace of mind. Whoever has made a claim takes precedence when solutions are considered.\r\n\r\nYou can always propose your own funded project, if you would like to contribute something of value that is not yet covered by an official bounty.\r\n</details>\r\n\r\n# Implement a new interactive example [$400]\r\n\r\nWe have a growing collection of interactive examples in this repository, showcasing a variety of interesting networking setups and their dynamics. To claim this bounty propose, discuss, and implement new examples of a networking simulations of interest to you. Multiple people can claim this bounty repeatedly with different projects.\r\n\r\nSubmissions will have to be well documented and tested, in a format that makes them as easy to run as the already existing examples.\r\n\r\nSome examples can be seen running online at https://areweentangledyet.com/\r\n\r\n**Required skills**: Knowledge of the phenomenon or protocol being simulated in the example, comfort with visualization libraries like Makie.\r\n\r\n**Reviewer**: Stefan Krastanov\r\n\r\n**Duration**: 2 months\r\n\r\n#### Payout procedure:\r\n\r\nThe Funding for these bounties comes from the National Science Foundation and from the NSF Center for Quantum Networks. The payouts are managed by the NumFOCUS foundation and processed in bulk once every two months. If you live in a country in which NumFOCUS can make payments, you can participate in this bounty program.\r\n\r\n[Click here for more details about the bug bounty program.](https://github.com/QuantumSavory/.github/blob/main/BUG_BOUNTIES.md)","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/QuantumSavory/QuantumSavory.jl/issues/138/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/QuantumSavory/QuantumSavory.jl/issues/138/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/QuantumSavory/QuantumSavory.jl/issues/137","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/QuantumSavory/QuantumSavory.jl","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/QuantumSavory/QuantumSavory.jl/issues/137/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/QuantumSavory/QuantumSavory.jl/issues/137/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/QuantumSavory/QuantumSavory.jl/issues/137/events","html_url":"https://github.com/QuantumSavory/QuantumSavory.jl/issues/137","id":2441265567,"node_id":"I_kwDOHgUEFc6RgsGf","number":137,"title":"Implement a networking protocol primitive [$400]","user":{"login":"Krastanov","id":705248,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNTI0OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/705248?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov","html_url":"https://github.com/Krastanov","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":7183765090,"node_id":"LA_kwDOHgUEFc8AAAABrC-OYg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/QuantumSavory/QuantumSavory.jl/labels/bug%20bounty","name":"bug bounty","color":"47F5AC","default":false,"description":"There is an award for solving this issue."},{"id":7183794196,"node_id":"LA_kwDOHgUEFc8AAAABrDAAFA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/QuantumSavory/QuantumSavory.jl/labels/bounty:400","name":"bounty:400","color":"86C87A","default":false,"description":""}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":13,"created_at":"2024-08-01T01:58:12Z","updated_at":"2026-05-17T12:57:42Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"<details>\r\n<summary><strong>Bug bounty logistic details</strong> (click to expand)</summary>\r\n\r\nTo claim exclusive time to work on this bounty either post a comment here or message [skrastanov@umass.edu](mailto:skrastanov@umass.edu) with:\r\n\r\n- your name\r\n- github username\r\n- **(optional)** a brief list of previous pertinent projects you have engaged in\r\n\r\nCurrently the project is claimed by `no one` until `...`.\r\n\r\nIf you want to, you can work on this project without making a claim, however claims are encouraged to give you and other contributors peace of mind. Whoever has made a claim takes precedence when solutions are considered.\r\n\r\nYou can always propose your own funded project, if you would like to contribute something of value that is not yet covered by an official bounty.\r\n</details>\r\n\r\n# Implement a networking protocol primitive [$400]\r\n\r\nThere are many interesting protocols and networking primitives yet to be added to this library. To claim this bounty propose and then implement a protocol for the ProtocolZoo submodule. Multiple people can claim this bounty (repeatedly) for new implementations. For substantial development efforts bigger bounties can be approved.\r\n\r\nTests and documentation have to be part of such submissions.\r\n\r\n**Required skills**: Deep knowledge of the protocol being implemented and rough understanding of networking simulations with this library.\r\n\r\n**Reviewer**: Stefan Krastanov\r\n\r\n**Duration**: 2 months\r\n\r\n**Publication**: In the next 2 years we plan to release a paper in a selective journal about this software. Contributing to this issue would deserve a co-authorship status on such a paper (if the contributor so desires)\r\n\r\n#### Payout procedure:\r\n\r\nThe Funding for these bounties comes from the National Science Foundation and from the NSF Center for Quantum Networks. The payouts are managed by the NumFOCUS foundation and processed in bulk once every two months. If you live in a country in which NumFOCUS can make payments, you can participate in this bounty program.\r\n\r\n[Click here for more details about the bug bounty program.](https://github.com/QuantumSavory/.github/blob/main/BUG_BOUNTIES.md)","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/QuantumSavory/QuantumSavory.jl/issues/137/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/QuantumSavory/QuantumSavory.jl/issues/137/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stashapp/stash/issues/4467","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stashapp/stash","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stashapp/stash/issues/4467/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stashapp/stash/issues/4467/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stashapp/stash/issues/4467/events","html_url":"https://github.com/stashapp/stash/issues/4467","id":2085987070,"node_id":"I_kwDOCBp0tM58VaL-","number":4467,"title":"Ability to scrape scene markers","user":{"login":"Maista6969","id":131594657,"node_id":"U_kgDOB9f5oQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/131594657?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Maista6969","html_url":"https://github.com/Maista6969","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Maista6969/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Maista6969/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Maista6969/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Maista6969/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Maista6969/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Maista6969/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Maista6969/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Maista6969/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Maista6969/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":3836749486,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzODM2NzQ5NDg2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stashapp/stash/labels/feature%20request","name":"feature request","color":"a2eeef","default":false,"description":"User request for a feature or functionality"}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2024-01-17T11:27:06Z","updated_at":"2026-05-16T12:45:55Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Some sites and networks offer marker data for their scenes, most often through their API. Currently this can only be exploited by `sceneByFragment` script scrapers as they can use the Stash GQL API to query for extra information about the current scene and then subsequent mutations to add markers. This is not possible for URL scrapers since they do not receive any information about the scene they are scraping\r\n\r\nI don't like the idea of marker scraping being limited to script scrapers, nor of scrapers needing to do this extra work for something that should be Stash's responsibility. The fact that this adds markers to a scene even before the user has reviewed the scrape results in the UI can also be unfortunate.\r\n\r\nI think a scraper could return markers in the following format, with an example for the birthday party that starts at 2 minutes into the video:\r\n```json\r\n{\r\n  \"name\": \"Birthday Party\",\r\n  \"start\": 120,\r\n  \"end\": 155,\r\n  \"primaryTag\": \"Celebration\",\r\n  \"secondaryTags\": [\"Cake\", \"Gay Ol' Time\"]\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nWhen presenting this in the UI these markers could be shown in the same style as tags and the user could choose which ones they wanted to import exactly like tags behave today: the only thing that would be different is that markers have secondary tags and I can't think of a nice clean way to display that","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stashapp/stash/issues/4467/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stashapp/stash/issues/4467/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/8688","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/8688/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/8688/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/8688/events","html_url":"https://github.com/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/8688","id":4388298917,"node_id":"I_kwDORGgqa88AAAABBZAgpQ","number":8688,"title":"[UTXO-BUG] 4 Vulnerabilities: Unlimited Minting, Epoch Crash, Orphaned Mempool, Unvalidated Data Inputs","user":{"login":"ahmadfardan464-cmyk","id":246840370,"node_id":"U_kgDODrZ8Mg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/246840370?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ahmadfardan464-cmyk","html_url":"https://github.com/ahmadfardan464-cmyk","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ahmadfardan464-cmyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ahmadfardan464-cmyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ahmadfardan464-cmyk/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ahmadfardan464-cmyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ahmadfardan464-cmyk/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ahmadfardan464-cmyk/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ahmadfardan464-cmyk/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ahmadfardan464-cmyk/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ahmadfardan464-cmyk/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":5,"created_at":"2026-05-06T02:22:08Z","updated_at":"2026-05-08T06:47:09Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"# RustChain UTXO Bug Bounty Report\n\n**Submitted by:** Bitbot (Beacon Agent bcn_b13fb9df30e4)  \n**Date:** 2026-05-06  \n**Target:** [RustChain UTXO Implementation](https://github.com/Scottcjn/Rustchain/tree/main/node)  \n**Bounty:** [#2819 — Red Team UTXO Implementation (50-200 RTC)](https://github.com/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/2819)\n\n---\n\n## 🔴 CRITICAL: Unlimited Coin Minting via Repeated mining_reward Transactions (200 RTC)\n\n### Vulnerability Class\nFund creation from nothing (Critical — Bounty tier: 200 RTC)\n\n### Description\n`apply_transaction()` does not enforce a per-block coinbase limit. While it correctly checks that `output_total <= MAX_COINBASE_OUTPUT_NRTC` per individual transaction, an attacker who can call `apply_transaction()` with `_allow_minting=True` can create **unlimited** mining_reward transactions at the same `block_height`, each minting up to `MAX_COINBASE_OUTPUT_NRTC` (1.5 RTC per block × 144 blocks = 216 RTC).\n\nThis means a single block can have multiple coinbase transactions, each creating new RTC from nothing.\n\n### Root Cause\nIn `utxo_db.py`, `apply_transaction()` (line ~358):\n```python\nMINTING_TX_TYPES = {'mining_reward'}\nif tx_type in MINTING_TX_TYPES and not tx.get('_allow_minting'):\n    return False\n```\n\nThe check only verifies that `_allow_minting` is set for mining_reward transactions. There is **no check** that:\n1. Only one coinbase transaction exists per block\n2. The total minted per block doesn't exceed the protocol limit\n3. The `_allow_minting` flag can't be set by any code path\n\n### PoC\n```python\ndb = UtxoDB(':memory:')\ndb.init_tables()\n\n# Mint 100 coinbase transactions in block 1 — each creates 1 RTC from nothing\nfor i in range(100):\n    mint_tx = {\n        'tx_type': 'mining_reward',\n        'inputs': [],\n        'outputs': [{'address': f'attacker_{i}', 'value_nrtc': 1 * UNIT}],\n        'fee_nrtc': 0,\n        'timestamp': int(time.time()),\n        '_allow_minting': True,\n    }\n    db.apply_transaction(mint_tx, block_height=1)\n\n# Result: 100 RTC created from nothing in a single block\nintegrity = db.integrity_check()\n# integrity['total_unspent_rtc'] == 100.0 — should be at most ~1.5 RTC per block\n```\n\n### Impact\n- **Unlimited inflation**: Attacker can mint arbitrary amounts of RTC\n- **Consensus failure**: Different nodes could have different total supplies if they process different numbers of coinbase transactions\n- **State root divergence**: Each minting creates different UTXO boxes, causing state root mismatch\n\n### Suggested Fix\nAdd a per-block coinbase limit check:\n```python\n# In apply_transaction(), after the minting type check:\nif tx_type in MINTING_TX_TYPES:\n    # Check if a coinbase already exists for this block\n    existing = conn.execute(\n        \"SELECT COUNT(*) FROM utxo_transactions WHERE block_height = ? AND tx_type = 'mining_reward'\",\n        (block_height,)\n    ).fetchone()[0]\n    if existing > 0:\n        return abort()  # Only one coinbase per block\n```\n\n---\n\n## 🔴 HIGH: Epoch Settlement Crashes — UtxoDB() Missing db_path (100 RTC)\n\n### Vulnerability Class\nRace condition / broken code path (High — Bounty tier: 100 RTC)\n\n### Description\nIn `rustchain_v2_integrated_v2.2.1_rip200.py`, line 2882:\n```python\nUtxoDB().apply_transaction(utxo_tx, epoch * 144, conn=conn)\n```\n\n`UtxoDB()` is called **without the required `db_path` argument**. The `UtxoDB.__init__` signature is `def __init__(self, db_path: str)`, so this call raises `TypeError`, which is caught by the surrounding `except Exception`, causing the **entire epoch settlement to ROLLBACK**.\n\nThis means:\n- Mining rewards are NEVER distributed via UTXO dual-write\n- The account-model balance update (line 2874) is also rolled back\n- No miners receive rewards when `UTXO_DUAL_WRITE` is enabled\n- The epoch is never marked as settled (line 2888 is never reached)\n\n### Verified\n```python\nfrom utxo_db import UtxoDB\ntry:\n    UtxoDB()\nexcept TypeError as e:\n    print(e)  # \"UtxoDB.__init__() missing 1 required positional argument: 'db_path'\"\n```\n\n### Impact\n- **Complete reward distribution failure**: Miners earn nothing\n- **Epoch settlement never completes**: `epoch_state.settled` stays 0\n- **Repeated retry**: Epoch settlement is retried on every cycle, each time crashing\n- **Account model corruption**: The ROLLBACK undoes the account balance update too\n\n### Suggested Fix\n```python\n# Line 2882: Use the module-level _utxo_db instance instead of UtxoDB()\n_utxo_db.apply_transaction(utxo_tx, epoch * 144, conn=conn)\n```\nOr create with db_path:\n```python\nUtxoDB(DB_PATH).apply_transaction(utxo_tx, epoch * 144, conn=conn)\n```\n\n---\n\n## 🟡 MEDIUM: Orphaned Mempool Claims After Main-Chain Spend (50 RTC)\n\n### Vulnerability Class\nMempool DoS / stale claim persistence (Medium — Bounty tier: 50 RTC)\n\n### Description\nWhen a UTXO box is claimed by a mempool transaction and then spent on the main chain (by a different, confirmed transaction), the mempool input claim is **not cleaned up**. This creates an orphaned claim that persists until the mempool entry expires (`MAX_TX_AGE_SECONDS = 3600`).\n\nDuring this window, the orphaned claim incorrectly reports the box as \"double-spend pending\" via `mempool_check_double_spend()`, even though the box is already spent in the confirmed chain.\n\n### Root Cause\n`apply_transaction()` spends UTXO boxes on the main chain but does **not** remove corresponding mempool input claims. There is no cross-layer cleanup between confirmed transactions and mempool entries.\n\nIn `utxo_db.py`, `apply_transaction()` (line ~475):\n```python\n# -- spend inputs ------------------------------------------------\nfor inp in inputs:\n    updated = conn.execute(\n        \"\"\"UPDATE utxo_boxes SET spent_at = ?, spent_by_tx = ?\n           WHERE box_id = ? AND spent_at IS NULL\"\"\",\n        (now, tx_id_hex, inp['box_id']),\n    ).rowcount\n    # ... but NO cleanup of mempool claims for this box_id\n```\n\n### PoC\n```python\ndb = UtxoDB(':memory:')\ndb.init_tables()\nbox = create_genesis_box(db, \"alice\", 10 * UNIT)\n\n# Add TX to mempool claiming the box\ntx_mempool = {\n    'tx_id': 'mempool_tx_1',\n    'tx_type': 'transfer',\n    'inputs': [{'box_id': box['box_id'], 'spending_proof': 'x'}],\n    'outputs': [{'address': 'bob', 'value_nrtc': 10 * UNIT}],\n    'fee_ntc': 0,\n    'timestamp': int(time.time()),\n}\ndb.mempool_add(tx_mempool)  # True\n\n# Spend the box on main chain (different TX)\ntx_main = {\n    'tx_type': 'transfer',\n    'inputs': [{'box_id': box['box_id'], 'spending_proof': 'x'}],\n    'outputs': [{'address': 'carol', 'value_nrtc': 10 * UNIT}],\n    'fee_nrtc': 0,\n    'timestamp': int(time.time()),\n}\ndb.apply_transaction(tx_main, block_height=1)  # True\n\n# The box is now spent, but mempool still claims it\ndb.mempool_check_double_spend(box['box_id'])  # True — WRONG! Box is already spent\n```\n\n### Impact\n- **DoS vector**: Orphaned mempool claims can block legitimate transactions for up to 1 hour\n- **Stale state**: `mempool_check_double_spend()` returns incorrect results\n- **Mempool pollution**: Orphaned entries waste mempool slots (max `MAX_POOL_SIZE = 10,000`)\n\n### Suggested Fix\nAfter spending a box in `apply_transaction()`, also remove its mempool claims:\n```python\n# After spending inputs, clean up mempool claims\nfor inp in inputs:\n    conn.execute(\n        \"DELETE FROM utxo_mempool_inputs WHERE box_id = ?\",\n        (inp['box_id'],)\n    )\n    # Also remove the mempool TX that claimed this input\n    # (or mark it as invalid)\n```\n\n---\n\n## 🟡 MEDIUM: Data Inputs Not Validated Against UTXO Set (25-50 RTC)\n\n### Vulnerability Class\nState manipulation / data integrity (Low-Medium — Bounty tier: 25-50 RTC)\n\n### Description\nThe `data_inputs` field in transactions is stored without any validation. A transaction can reference non-existent box IDs as data inputs, and they are accepted and recorded in the transaction log.\n\nWhile data inputs are \"read-only\" (not spent), they are intended to reference existing UTXO boxes that the transaction wants to read. Allowing phantom references could:\n1. Manipulate state root computation if data inputs affect Merkle tree\n2. Create misleading on-chain records\n3. Enable oracle manipulation attacks in smart contracts that verify data input existence\n\n### PoC\n```python\ntx = {\n    'tx_type': 'transfer',\n    'inputs': [{'box_id': real_box_id, 'spending_proof': 'x'}],\n    'outputs': [{'address': 'bob', 'value_nrtc': 10 * UNIT}],\n    'data_inputs': ['phantom_box_id_that_does_not_exist'],\n    'fee_nrtc': 0,\n    'timestamp': int(time.time()),\n}\ndb.apply_transaction(tx, block_height=1)  # True — accepted without validation\n```\n\n### Suggested Fix\nValidate data inputs exist and are unspent:\n```python\n# In apply_transaction(), after input validation:\nfor di in tx.get('data_inputs', []):\n    row = conn.execute(\n        \"SELECT spent_at FROM utxo_boxes WHERE box_id = ?\",\n        (di,),\n    ).fetchone()\n    if not row:\n        return abort()  # Data input must reference existing box\n    if row['spent_at'] is not None:\n        return abort()  # Data input must be unspent\n```\n\n---\n\n## Summary\n\n| # | Severity | Bug | Bounty Tier | Status |\n|---|----------|-----|-------------|--------|\n| 1 | 🔴 Critical | Unlimited coin minting (no per-block coinbase limit) | 200 RTC | Confirmed |\n| 2 | 🔴 High | Epoch settlement crashes (UtxoDB() missing db_path) | 100 RTC | Confirmed |\n| 3 | 🟡 Medium | Orphaned mempool claims after main-chain spend | 50 RTC | Confirmed |\n| 4 | 🟡 Medium | Data inputs not validated against UTXO set | 25-50 RTC | Confirmed |\n\n**Total potential bounty: 375-400 RTC**\n\nAll bugs have been verified with executable PoC tests against the current codebase (main branch, commit fe2cdd7781).","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/8688/reactions","total_count":7,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":3,"eyes":1},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/8688/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/niftymonkey/champ-sage/issues/117","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/niftymonkey/champ-sage","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/niftymonkey/champ-sage/issues/117/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/niftymonkey/champ-sage/issues/117/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/niftymonkey/champ-sage/issues/117/events","html_url":"https://github.com/niftymonkey/champ-sage/issues/117","id":4314045679,"node_id":"I_kwDORrCsXs8AAAABASMc7w","number":117,"title":"Enforce item-purchase legality across all restriction types in build paths","user":{"login":"niftymonkey","id":848981,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg0ODk4MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/848981?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/niftymonkey","html_url":"https://github.com/niftymonkey","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/niftymonkey/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/niftymonkey/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/niftymonkey/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/niftymonkey/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/niftymonkey/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/niftymonkey/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/niftymonkey/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/niftymonkey/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/niftymonkey/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":10466245731,"node_id":"LA_kwDORrCsXs8AAAACb9Y8Yw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/niftymonkey/champ-sage/labels/bug","name":"bug","color":"d73a4a","default":true,"description":"Something isn't working"}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/niftymonkey/champ-sage/milestones/1","html_url":"https://github.com/niftymonkey/champ-sage/milestone/1","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/niftymonkey/champ-sage/milestones/1/labels","id":15210242,"node_id":"MI_kwDORrCsXs4A6BcC","number":1,"title":"Phase 1 - POC","description":"Proof of concept — validates AI recommendation quality and voice-first interaction model","creator":{"login":"niftymonkey","id":848981,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg0ODk4MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/848981?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/niftymonkey","html_url":"https://github.com/niftymonkey","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/niftymonkey/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/niftymonkey/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/niftymonkey/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/niftymonkey/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/niftymonkey/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/niftymonkey/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/niftymonkey/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/niftymonkey/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/niftymonkey/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":7,"closed_issues":63,"state":"open","created_at":"2026-03-19T07:24:16Z","updated_at":"2026-05-22T23:37:00Z","due_on":null,"closed_at":null},"comments":1,"created_at":"2026-04-23T06:40:44Z","updated_at":"2026-05-08T05:05:14Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Description\n\nThe LLM-generated build path can recommend combinations of items that the player cannot legally own simultaneously. #109 addressed one narrow case (two pairs of boots); this ticket is the general rule.\n\nLeague item legality has two layers: **mode/queue availability** (which items exist in the current pool) and **per-item purchase restrictions** (which items cannot coexist in a 6-slot inventory). A build-path recommendation is only valid if every item passes both layers, accounting for the player's current inventory and any upgrade-path exceptions.\n\n### Full rule set\n\nItem legality is determined by two layers:\n\n**1. Mode / queue item pool**\n- An item must be available in the current game mode.\n- Different modes can have different item pools.\n- Some modes may include mode-exclusive or temporary items.\n\n**2. Per-item purchase restrictions**\n- Some items belong to restricted item groups.\n- If two items share the same relevant restriction, they cannot both be owned at the same time.\n- An upgrade path is allowed when the resulting item consumes the earlier component.\n\n**Restriction types:**\n- **Boots restriction** — only one Boots item at a time (mode-specific boots count).\n- **Item-group restriction** — mutually exclusive families (Spellblade, Hydra, Lifeline, and others defined by current patch data).\n- **Duplicate Legendary restriction** — only one copy of a given Legendary.\n\n**Examples of illegal recommendations:**\n- A second pair of boots.\n- Two items from the same restricted group (e.g. Trinity Force + Essence Reaver).\n- An item not available in the current mode.\n- An Arena-exclusive or event-specific item in the wrong mode.\n- A second copy of the same Legendary.\n\n## Why\n\nInvalid entries waste slots in the primary deliverable at the top of the coaching panel and undermine trust in the recommendations. The schema enum (#108 phase 4) ensures every `buildPath[].name` is a catalog entry, but catalog membership alone does not imply two entries can legally coexist — that requires cross-item reasoning the schema cannot express.\n\n## Approach\n\n- **Data source:** stay on DDragon. Detect boots via the existing `Boots` tag. Detect mutex item groups by parsing `<passive>...</passive>` markers in item descriptions (Spellblade, Hydra, Lifeline, etc.). Detect duplicate Legendaries by name equality. Mode availability is already filtered upstream via `maps`.\n- **Remediation:** validate after the LLM returns. On any violation, issue one corrective LLM call showing the offending path and the broken rule. If the retry still violates, ship the 6 items and log a warning. No silent drops or placeholders.\n- **Eval coverage:** #109 shipped a `Boots Uniqueness` gate scorer in `coaching.eval.ts`. When this ticket lands, retire that scorer and replace it with a broader `Item Legality` gate scorer that exercises every restriction type (boots, mutex groups, duplicate Legendary, mode availability) — the narrow scorer becomes redundant once the general rule is enforced.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Build paths never contain two items that cannot legally coexist under any known restriction type (boots, mutex group, duplicate legendary).\n- [ ] Build paths never contain items unavailable in the current game mode.\n- [ ] Mode-exclusive items (Arena, event queues) are only recommended in their valid modes.\n- [ ] Upgrade-path transitions (component → finished item) are not flagged as violations.\n- [ ] Violations are corrected via one retry before the plan is surfaced to the player.\n\n## Related\n\nFollows #109 (boots-only subset).\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/niftymonkey/champ-sage/issues/117/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/niftymonkey/champ-sage/issues/117/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opencv/opencv/issues/16433","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opencv/opencv","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opencv/opencv/issues/16433/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opencv/opencv/issues/16433/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opencv/opencv/issues/16433/events","html_url":"https://github.com/opencv/opencv/issues/16433","id":555108082,"node_id":"MDU6SXNzdWU1NTUxMDgwODI=","number":16433,"title":"GpuMat as input/output to cv::dnn::Net","user":{"login":"YashasSamaga","id":6652578,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2NTI1Nzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6652578?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/YashasSamaga","html_url":"https://github.com/YashasSamaga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YashasSamaga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YashasSamaga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YashasSamaga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YashasSamaga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YashasSamaga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YashasSamaga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YashasSamaga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YashasSamaga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YashasSamaga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":241023000,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNDEwMjMwMDA=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opencv/opencv/labels/feature","name":"feature","color":"84b6eb","default":false,"description":null},{"id":241030002,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNDEwMzAwMDI=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opencv/opencv/labels/category:%20gpu/cuda%20(contrib)","name":"category: gpu/cuda (contrib)","color":"606060","default":false,"description":"OpenCV 4.0+: moved to opencv_contrib"},{"id":297279980,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyOTcyNzk5ODA=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opencv/opencv/labels/RFC","name":"RFC","color":"f080f0","default":false,"description":null},{"id":481214924,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw0ODEyMTQ5MjQ=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opencv/opencv/labels/future","name":"future","color":"d4c5f9","default":false,"description":"This issue can't be fixed during restrictions of the compatibility requirements"},{"id":635087908,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw2MzUwODc5MDg=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opencv/opencv/labels/category:%20dnn","name":"category: dnn","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null},{"id":1007448297,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxMDA3NDQ4Mjk3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opencv/opencv/labels/effort:%20few%20weeks","name":"effort: few weeks","color":"409040","default":false,"description":"Contribution / porting of a new/existed algorithm. With samples / tests / docs / tutorials"}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opencv/opencv/milestones/63","html_url":"https://github.com/opencv/opencv/milestone/63","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opencv/opencv/milestones/63/labels","id":15831875,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAE3xU84A8ZND","number":63,"title":"5.1","description":"","creator":{"login":"asmorkalov","id":2536374,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1MzYzNzQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2536374?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmorkalov","html_url":"https://github.com/asmorkalov","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmorkalov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmorkalov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmorkalov/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmorkalov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmorkalov/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmorkalov/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmorkalov/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmorkalov/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmorkalov/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":123,"closed_issues":50,"state":"open","created_at":"2026-05-07T13:22:39Z","updated_at":"2026-07-07T06:14:27Z","due_on":null,"closed_at":null},"comments":42,"created_at":"2020-01-25T16:56:11Z","updated_at":"2026-05-07T13:28:16Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### System information (version)\r\n- OpenCV => 4.2.0\r\n\r\n##### APIs that need changes\r\n\r\nSuitable APIs for `GpuMat` input:\r\n1. `void setInput(InputArray blob, const String& name = \"\", double scalefactor = 1.0, const Scalar& mean = Scalar());`\r\n\r\nSuitable APIs for `GpuMat` output:\r\n1. `void forward(OutputArrayOfArrays outputBlobs, const String& outputName = String());`\r\n2. `void forward(OutputArrayOfArrays outputBlobs, const std::vector<String>& outBlobNames);`\r\n\r\nModifications to support `GpuMat`:\r\n\r\n1. `void blobFromImage(InputArray image, OutputArray blob, double scalefactor=1.0, const Size& size = Size(), const Scalar& mean = Scalar(), bool swapRB=false, bool crop=false, int ddepth=CV_32F);`\r\n\r\nMight also require a new API that would allow a stream to be specified (required if `blobFromImage` needs to be performed asynchronously).\r\n\r\nThe CUDA backend uses fully packed tensors everywhere and expects a fully packed tensor as input. `GpuMat` given as input might be using a 2D memory layout which may not be contiguous. `blobFromImage` must return a contiguous copy of the input.\r\n\r\nThe outputs of the CUDA backend are also in fully packed tensors. Hence, for further optimal use of the output (in the case it's an image) would require a transformation to 2D memory layout.\r\n\r\n##### Problems:\r\n1. `GpuMat` cannot store an arbitrary number of dimensions. How can the batch of images be passed?\r\n\r\n\r\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opencv/opencv/issues/16433/reactions","total_count":13,"+1":13,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opencv/opencv/issues/16433/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/home-assistant/core/issues/146155","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/home-assistant/core","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/home-assistant/core/issues/146155/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/home-assistant/core/issues/146155/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/home-assistant/core/issues/146155/events","html_url":"https://github.com/home-assistant/core/issues/146155","id":3117465587,"node_id":"I_kwDOAMSroc650L_z","number":146155,"title":"Roomba 505 Plus can't be added to Home Asssistant.","user":{"login":"microbi0","id":82952493,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgyOTUyNDkz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/82952493?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/microbi0","html_url":"https://github.com/microbi0","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/microbi0/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/microbi0/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/microbi0/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/microbi0/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/microbi0/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/microbi0/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/microbi0/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/microbi0/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/microbi0/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":653810068,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw2NTM4MTAwNjg=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/home-assistant/core/labels/integration:%20roomba","name":"integration: roomba","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":88,"created_at":"2025-06-04T11:17:55Z","updated_at":"2026-05-05T20:59:17Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":{"id":1798639,"node_id":"IT_kwDOANNB784AG3Hv","name":"Bug","description":"An unexpected problem or behavior","color":"red","created_at":"2024-01-25T14:53:42Z","updated_at":"2024-07-26T10:31:18Z","is_enabled":true},"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### The problem\n\nI just bought a Roomba Plus 505 Combo (the most recent models) and I'm unable to add it to Home Assistant, even trying the manual way. I can retreive the password but, it always rejects it. \n\nIs there any problem with the integration or the newer models aren't compatible with it? If not, can we expect this anytime soon? \n\n### What version of Home Assistant Core has the issue?\n\ncore-2025.5.3\n\n### What was the last working version of Home Assistant Core?\n\n_No response_\n\n### What type of installation are you running?\n\nHome Assistant OS\n\n### Integration causing the issue\n\niRobot Roomba and Braava\n\n### Link to integration documentation on our website\n\nhttps://www.home-assistant.io/integrations/roomba/#retrieving-your-credentials\n\n### Diagnostics information\n\n_No response_\n\n### Example YAML snippet\n\n```yaml\n\n```\n\n### Anything in the logs that might be useful for us?\n\n```txt\n\n```\n\n### Additional information\n\n_No response_","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/home-assistant/core/issues/146155/reactions","total_count":4,"+1":4,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/home-assistant/core/issues/146155/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/LennyMalcolm0/bitcoin/issues/30","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/LennyMalcolm0/bitcoin","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/LennyMalcolm0/bitcoin/issues/30/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/LennyMalcolm0/bitcoin/issues/30/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/LennyMalcolm0/bitcoin/issues/30/events","html_url":"https://github.com/LennyMalcolm0/bitcoin/issues/30","id":2846803123,"node_id":"I_kwDON4Cbcc6prsSz","number":30,"title":"Optimize code for performance and efficiency. ($400)","user":{"login":"LennyMalcolm0","id":113526852,"node_id":"U_kgDOBsRIRA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/113526852?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/LennyMalcolm0","html_url":"https://github.com/LennyMalcolm0","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LennyMalcolm0/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LennyMalcolm0/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LennyMalcolm0/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LennyMalcolm0/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LennyMalcolm0/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LennyMalcolm0/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LennyMalcolm0/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LennyMalcolm0/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LennyMalcolm0/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":9008105829,"node_id":"LA_kwDON4Cbcc8AAAACGOzJZQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/LennyMalcolm0/bitcoin/labels/%F0%9F%92%B5%20Bounty","name":"💵 Bounty","color":"85BB65","default":false,"description":"Issues with a monetary reward"}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2025-02-11T23:43:06Z","updated_at":"2026-05-04T03:29:21Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Accept task [here](https://devasign.com/developer/a09e0f4c-08e9-4492-ae13-6fea7aa1dd08).\n\n**Description:** Refactor and optimize code to improve processing speed and reduce resource consumption.\n\n**Timeline:** 3 weeks\n\n**Bounty:** 400 USD","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/LennyMalcolm0/bitcoin/issues/30/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/LennyMalcolm0/bitcoin/issues/30/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Honest-Protocol/Gitcoin_Metamorphosis/issues/5","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Honest-Protocol/Gitcoin_Metamorphosis","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Honest-Protocol/Gitcoin_Metamorphosis/issues/5/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Honest-Protocol/Gitcoin_Metamorphosis/issues/5/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Honest-Protocol/Gitcoin_Metamorphosis/issues/5/events","html_url":"https://github.com/Honest-Protocol/Gitcoin_Metamorphosis/issues/5","id":1369170402,"node_id":"I_kwDOH-q5yM5Rm-Hi","number":5,"title":"Data Visualization Bounty","user":{"login":"ck-convex","id":92904866,"node_id":"U_kgDOBYmdog","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92904866?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ck-convex","html_url":"https://github.com/ck-convex","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ck-convex/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ck-convex/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ck-convex/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ck-convex/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ck-convex/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ck-convex/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ck-convex/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ck-convex/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ck-convex/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":3,"created_at":"2022-09-12T02:05:57Z","updated_at":"2026-05-01T04:31:01Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Prize Title\r\n\r\nEthereum Data Visualization Bounty\r\n\r\n### Prize Bounty\r\n\r\n- 1st - 1000 USDC & 1 Vigilante NFT \r\n- 2nd - 600 USDC \r\n- 3rd - 400 USDC\r\n\r\n### Challenge Description\r\n\r\nIn this bounty, participants will be tasked with visualizing datasets in unique ways that show interesting insights. Any available datasets can be used (ie existing Dune queries, data sets from other platforms) but data visualizations should focus on assets, addresses, contracts, and transactions on the Ethereum blockchain. Although, data type and methodology are up to the participant, data collection should be focused in 3 areas: security, compliance, and authenticity.\r\n\r\n- For security, think stolen NFTs, phishing, malware, etc. \r\n- For compliance, think AML, sanctions, etc. \r\n- For authenticity, think copycat NFTs, copycat tokens, DID, etc.\r\n\r\n### Submission Requirements\r\n\r\nData visualizations can be based on any tool the participant sees fit to utilize. Visualizations should be focused on data associated with assets, addresses, contracts, and transactions on the Ethereum blockchain. A description of the data collection process should also be included. Data can be submitted via Github, Dune, or any public platform. Any available datasets can be used (ie existing Dune queries, data sets from other platforms). For example, other hackathon submissions (ie data collection datasets) are available to use.\r\n\r\nSubmissions not focused on security, compliance, or authenticity will be disregarded.\r\n\r\nParticipants are allowed unlimited submissions. Each submission will be counted individually and participants are eligible to win multiple prizes.\r\n\r\n### Judging Criteria\r\n\r\nSubmissions will be judged on the following criteria; however, judges will use their discretion in choosing winners:\r\n\r\n- Relevancy: Is the visualization relevant to the categories of security, compliance, and authenticity? \r\n- Quality: Is the visualization clear? Are the relevant insights clear? \r\n- Uniqueness of data: Did other participants submit similar datasets? \r\n- Insights: Can interesting insights be drawn based on the visualization?\r\n\r\n### Winner Announcement Date\r\n\r\nWinners will be announced by October 6th, 2022.\r\n\r\n### Resources\r\n\r\nQuestions? <br>\r\nhttps://discord.gg/VcxcmvWbg6\r\n\r\nHonest Protocol Resources <br>\r\nhttps://twitter.com/Honest_Protocol <br>\r\nhttps://www.honestprotocol.xyz/ <br>\r\nhttps://medium.com/@convexlabs\r\n\r\nDune Resources <br>\r\nhttps://dune.com/browse/dashboards <br>\r\nhttps://discord.gg/UQZudmeg4F","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Honest-Protocol/Gitcoin_Metamorphosis/issues/5/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Honest-Protocol/Gitcoin_Metamorphosis/issues/5/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/449","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/449/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/449/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/449/events","html_url":"https://github.com/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/449","id":3261051663,"node_id":"I_kwDOGM0Nh87CX7MP","number":449,"title":"A reliable idiomatic wrapper for networkx [$400]","user":{"login":"Krastanov","id":705248,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNTI0OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/705248?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov","html_url":"https://github.com/Krastanov","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":7487699452,"node_id":"LA_kwDOGM0Nh88AAAABvk05_A","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/labels/bounty","name":"bounty","color":"A6D60A","default":false,"description":"There is an award for solving this issue."},{"id":8998436339,"node_id":"LA_kwDOGM0Nh88AAAACGFk98w","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/labels/bounty:400","name":"bounty:400","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"description":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[{"login":"Syuizen","id":15939422,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1OTM5NDIy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15939422?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Syuizen","html_url":"https://github.com/Syuizen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Syuizen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Syuizen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Syuizen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Syuizen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Syuizen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Syuizen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Syuizen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Syuizen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Syuizen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}],"milestone":null,"comments":33,"created_at":"2025-07-24T19:45:53Z","updated_at":"2026-04-30T12:22:37Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":{"login":"Syuizen","id":15939422,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1OTM5NDIy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15939422?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Syuizen","html_url":"https://github.com/Syuizen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Syuizen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Syuizen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Syuizen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Syuizen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Syuizen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Syuizen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Syuizen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Syuizen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Syuizen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"# A reliable idiomatic `networkx` wrapper [$400]\n\nUsing networkx through PythonCall.jl is trivially easy. This bounty is mostly about creating a new NetworkX.jl wrapper (by using PythonCall.jl) that provides quality-of-life improvements, \n\n- [ ] Fast conversion and/or views between Graphs.jl types and the networkx structures\n- [ ] Complete Graph API support for the newly created networkx wrapper types (so that networkx types can be used in all already existing Graph.jl algorithms that do not peek behind the API)\n- [ ] use GraphsInterfaceChecker.jl in the test suite\n- [ ] Dispatch from operations defined in Graphs/GraphsMatching/GraphsOptim to networkx implementation. For instance if there is a pre-existing `Graphs.some_interesting_property(::AbstractGraph)` there should now be a new method defined in NetworkX `some_interesting_property(g::AbstractGraph, ::NXAlgorithm)` that dispatches to the networkx implementation. It should convert the `g` argument to networkx graphs if necessary.\n- [ ] If there is an algorithm defined in networkx that does not exist yet in Graphs.jl, it should be declared in Graphs.jl (just a function with docs but no methods), together with an error hint that NetworkX is necessary. Given the large scope of the library, this can be more of a proof-of-concept setup, documenting how to add everything, but not expecting everything to be added for completing the bounty. \n- [ ] Proper tests and documentation.\n- [ ] PRs on this topic have to be submitted with clean git histories and well compartmentalized for ease of review. \n\n**Required skills**: familiarity with the Graphs.jl API and understanding of the PythonCall package\n\n**Reviewer**: any Graphs.jl member with merge rights\n\n**Duration**: 3 months\n\n#### Payout procedure:\n\nThe Funding for these bounties comes from the National Science Foundation and from the NSF Center for Quantum Networks. The payouts are managed by the NumFOCUS foundation and processed in bulk once every two months. If you live in a country in which NumFOCUS can make payments, you can participate in this bounty program.\n\n[Click here for more details about the bug bounty program.](https://github.com/QuantumSavory/.github/blob/main/BUG_BOUNTIES.md)\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Bug bounty logistic details</strong> (click to expand)</summary>\n\nTo claim exclusive time to work on this bounty either post a comment here or message [skrastanov@umass.edu](mailto:skrastanov@umass.edu) with:\n\n- your name\n- github username\n- **(optional)** a brief list of previous pertinent projects you have engaged in\n\nIf you want to, you can work on this project without making a claim, however claims are encouraged to give you and other contributors peace of mind. Whoever has made a claim takes precedence when solutions are considered.\n\nYou can always propose your own funded project, if you would like to contribute something of value that is not yet covered by an official bounty.\n</details>\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/449/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/449/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enjoy-digital/litepcie/issues/20","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enjoy-digital/litepcie","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enjoy-digital/litepcie/issues/20/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enjoy-digital/litepcie/issues/20/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enjoy-digital/litepcie/issues/20/events","html_url":"https://github.com/enjoy-digital/litepcie/issues/20","id":445205359,"node_id":"MDU6SXNzdWU0NDUyMDUzNTk=","number":20,"title":"Support LitePCIe on Lattice ECP5 SERDES (with open toolchain)","user":{"login":"mithro","id":21212,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMjEy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21212?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mithro","html_url":"https://github.com/mithro","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mithro/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mithro/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mithro/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mithro/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mithro/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mithro/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mithro/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mithro/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mithro/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":257264655,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNTcyNjQ2NTU=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enjoy-digital/litepcie/labels/help-welcome%20:)","name":"help-welcome :)","color":"9cf196","default":false,"description":""},{"id":1978003614,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxOTc4MDAzNjE0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enjoy-digital/litepcie/labels/new-feature","name":"new-feature","color":"00bcd4","default":false,"description":""},{"id":6422127588,"node_id":"LA_kwDOAoGBdc8AAAABfsnj5A","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enjoy-digital/litepcie/labels/sponsor-welcome%20:)","name":"sponsor-welcome :)","color":"9cf196","default":false,"description":""}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":46,"created_at":"2019-05-16T23:50:40Z","updated_at":"2026-04-28T06:46:00Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"COLLABORATOR","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Original message/request\r\n\r\nI'm opening this bug to track the progress of this.\r\n\r\nIt is my understanding that;\r\n (a) Project Trellis has all the documentation on the Lattice ECP5 SERDES.\r\n (b) @whitequark [has gotten the Lattice ECP5 SERDES to lock onto the PCIe bit stream](https://twitter.com/whitequark/status/1060735927688015873).\r\n (c) There is still a lot of work left to do.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### Summary of Possible Funding and Work (last updated on **2025-01-09**):\r\n\r\n#### Total Bounty Pool:\r\n- **Current Offers**: **11,400 EUR** (400 + 1000 + 6000 + 2000 + 2000).\r\n- **Realistic Target**: **8000 EUR** (as suggested by @whitequark, but still considered low).\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### Summary Table\r\n\r\n#### Funders:\r\n| Developer              | Bounty Offer                     | Conditions/Requests                                                                 |\r\n|------------------------|----------------------------------|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\r\n| **@snajpa**            | 400 EUR (one-time?)               | Requests a summary of current progress and known issues.                           |\r\n| **@motylewski**         | 1000 EUR (upon completion by 2025)| Requires completion by **2025-06-30**.                                             |\r\n| **@madscientist159**  | 6000 EUR (conditional)           | Requires core to work on Arctic Tern and POWER9 systems, with MMIO support.        |\r\n| **@teknoman117**       | 2000 EUR                         | Core must be integrated with LitePCIe and demonstrated with MMAP on an ECP5 board.                                                       |\r\n| **@enjoy-digital**     | 2000 EUR                         | Core must be integrated with LitePCIe and demonstrated with MMAP on an ECP5 board. |\r\n\r\n#### Developers:\r\n| Developer              | Role                     | Conditions/Requests                                                                 |\r\n|------------------------|--------------------------|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\r\n| **@whitequark**        | Technical contributor    | Willing to work but requires **8000 EUR** (still considered low). Unlikely by H1 2025. |\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### Detailed Requests\r\n\r\n#### @motylewski:\r\n- **Request**: Sponsors development of a free ECP5-PCIe core with a free Verilog toolchain for **LFE5UM(G)**.\r\n- **Offer**:\r\n  - **Now**: One **LFE5UM-45F-VERSA-EVN(G)** eval board (250-400 EUR) OR **200 EUR** if no hardware is needed.\r\n  - **Upon Completion**: **800 EUR** if the deadline **2025-06-30** is met.\r\n- **Background**: Needs an open-source PCIe core with a Wishbone interface by July 2025 to avoid purchasing Lattice's core (837 USD/year).\r\n\r\n#### Raptor Engineering:\r\n- **Request**: Offers **6000 EUR**, conditional on:\r\n  1. Core works on **Arctic Tern platform** (ECP5-85 + 1GB RAM).\r\n  2. Functions as a PCIe slave on **POWER9 systems** (e.g., Blackbird).\r\n  3. Synthesizable and routable on POWER hosts without binary blobs.\r\n  4. Basic **MMIO support** (BAR mapping and Wishbone read/write).\r\n- **Additional Support**: Provides **Arctic Tern module, carrier, and Blackbird host** for development.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### Key Points\r\n- **Total Bounty Pool**: **11,400 EUR** (current offers), exceeding the realistic target of **8000 EUR**.\r\n- **Work**: **@whitequark** is willing to work but needs sufficient funding and is unlikely to complete by H1 2025.\r\n- **Hardware**: **@madscientist159** offers hardware support (Arctic Tern and Blackbird host).\r\n- **Deadline**: **2025-06-30** for @moylewski's offer; no strict deadline for others.\r\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enjoy-digital/litepcie/issues/20/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enjoy-digital/litepcie/issues/20/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"reopened","pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chutesai/chutes-miner/issues/128","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chutesai/chutes-miner","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chutesai/chutes-miner/issues/128/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chutesai/chutes-miner/issues/128/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chutesai/chutes-miner/issues/128/events","html_url":"https://github.com/chutesai/chutes-miner/issues/128","id":4336388625,"node_id":"I_kwDONLQZNc8AAAABAngKEQ","number":128,"title":"Request: scale_allowance bump for hotkey 5HMaexp...gKDB (SEV-SNP active, hidream idle, 0% GPU util)","user":{"login":"ArtificialXai","id":216447082,"node_id":"U_kgDODOa4ag","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/216447082?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArtificialXai","html_url":"https://github.com/ArtificialXai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArtificialXai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArtificialXai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArtificialXai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArtificialXai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArtificialXai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArtificialXai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArtificialXai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArtificialXai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArtificialXai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-27T14:13:23Z","updated_at":"2026-04-27T14:13:23Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Hi team — running chutes-miner on hotkey `5HMaexp8oudN42e6CSwSrVe47RodueM4U71Ecf1H6pU8gKDB` (`Architect-AH` org, ArtificialXai contributor here). Filing a request rather than DMing because there's a paper trail other affected miners can +1.\n\n## Setup\n\n- **Hotkey:** `5HMaexp8oudN42e6CSwSrVe47RodueM4U71Ecf1H6pU8gKDB`\n- **Coldkey:** `5H6X9HkhTjL8zQBKdUEnVwJH8ZTRyHYtQZqYaHhvwHW3VBh3`\n- **Server:** `ah-mining-h100` at `185.26.8.97`\n- **GPU:** NVIDIA H100 PCIe 80GB (114 SMs, verified)\n- **Validator:** `5Dt7HZ7Zpw4DppPxFM7Ke3Cm7sDAWhsZXmM5ZAmE7dSVJbcQ`\n- **Deployed:** 2026-04-14 (continuous, 21+ days uptime)\n- **K3s:** `v1.34.6+k3s1`, gepetto online, audit-exporter healthy\n- **Currently assigned:** `hidream` (chute_id `85d04ade-09bd-52f7-a033-fdb672879a2f`)\n\n## Stats from `/miner/stats`\n\n| Window | compute_seconds | compute_units | invocations | bounties |\n|--------|-----------------|---------------|-------------|----------|\n| past_hour | ~3,400 | ~1,150 | <2 | 0 |\n| past_day | ~79,000 | ~26,000 | <10 | 0 |\n| all_time | ~466k | ~130k | 6 | 1 |\n\n`hidream` is being kept warm via availability scoring but receives almost no inference traffic on this server. Live H100 GPU utilization is **0%** while the chute reports \"all deployments ... scaling would be unproductive\".\n\n## TEE attestation (active since 2026-04-24)\n\n- AMD SEV-SNP fully enabled (kernel 6.17 HWE on Ubuntu 25.10)\n- SYSCFG bit 24 (SNPEn)=1 across all 32 CPUs (verified via `rdmsr 0xc0010010`)\n- `kvm_amd: SEV-SNP enabled (ASIDs 1-199)` in dmesg\n- RMP table at physical address `0x43e00000`\n- BIOS: Secure Boot off, IOMMU on, virtualization on (Supermicro H13SSW + AMI 3.8 firmware)\n\n**Node labels visible in our cluster:**\n- `chutes/tee=true`\n- `chutes/sev-snp=true`\n- `chutes/gpu=true`\n- `chutes/worker=true`\n- `nvidia.com/gpu.present=true`\n\n**Public attestation beacon:** `http://185.26.8.97:8100` (returns full SNP report on `/health`)\n\n## What we're seeing in gepetto autoscale logs\n\nThese chutes log `No viable server to scale` against our hotkey every 15 seconds:\n\n**TEE candidates (we believe we now qualify):**\n- `b048fe26-...` GLM-5.1-TEE (~15.5x effective)\n- `6320ab82-9e94-5d63-8e38-d136f61dc157` Qwen/Qwen3-Coder-Next-TEE\n- `ce6a92e4-5c2f-5681-9742-c80a4447bbdf` MiniMaxAI/MiniMax-M2.5-TEE\n- `7c012636-e4fe-5f28-89de-407c21c9378e` tngtech/DeepSeek-TNG-R1T2-Chimera-TEE\n- `398651e1-5f85-5e50-a513-7c5324e8e839` deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V3.2-TEE\n- Multiple Qwen/Qwen3-32B-TEE / Qwen/Qwen3.5-397B-TEE / Kimi-K2.6-TEE / GLM-4.7-TEE / GLM-5-TEE / MiMo-V2-Flash-TEE\n\n**Non-TEE high-multiplier alternates:**\n- `d899b064-d9ae-5612-99e6-413e9136671b` GLM-5-Turbo (~13.1x effective)\n- `572bd930-...` GLM-4.7-FP8 (~5.4x, only 1 miner — least competition)\n\nAll show `scalable: False, scale_allowance: 0` for our hotkey, which suggests this is an assignment/allowance gate rather than a local TEE/GPU failure.\n\n## Asks\n\n1. Could you bump our `scale_allowance` for any qualified TEE chute or one of the non-TEE high-multiplier alternates (GLM-5-Turbo / GLM-4.7-FP8)?\n2. Is there any extra signal/config we should be surfacing for TEE chutes to start landing on our node, beyond the labels listed above?\n3. Is there a public dashboard or process where miners can see their per-chute `scale_allowance` and request adjustments? Right now the only signal we have is the gepetto debug log.\n\n## Audit-exporter fix already shipped (worth upstreaming)\n\nThe `audit-exporter` CronJob in the `chutes` namespace was silently broken on single-node GPU deployments because of two issues in the helm chart:\n\n1. `nodeSelector: kubernetes.io/hostname=chutes-miner-cpu-0` — blocks scheduling on single-node GPU clusters\n2. `serviceAccountName: default` — lacks RBAC to list pods (needed for `prometheus_uptime`)\n\nPatched locally in `/home/ubuntu/chutes-miner/charts/chutes-miner/templates/audit-exporter.cronjob.yaml` (removed selector + set SA to `chutes`). Audit reports now committing on-chain hourly. Happy to submit a PR upstream if useful — would help any other single-node GPU miners hitting the same silent failure.\n\n## Glad to share\n\nFull inventory dump, validator handshake logs, attestation signatures, or any other diagnostic. Just reply with what you'd like to see.\n\nThanks!\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chutesai/chutes-miner/issues/128/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chutesai/chutes-miner/issues/128/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/447","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/447/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/447/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/447/events","html_url":"https://github.com/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/447","id":3260998830,"node_id":"I_kwDOGM0Nh87CXuSu","number":447,"title":"A reliable idiomatic wrapper for the C++ library `LEMON` [$400]","user":{"login":"Krastanov","id":705248,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNTI0OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/705248?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov","html_url":"https://github.com/Krastanov","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":7487699452,"node_id":"LA_kwDOGM0Nh88AAAABvk05_A","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/labels/bounty","name":"bounty","color":"A6D60A","default":false,"description":"There is an award for solving this issue."},{"id":8998436339,"node_id":"LA_kwDOGM0Nh88AAAACGFk98w","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/labels/bounty:400","name":"bounty:400","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"description":null},{"id":9028522432,"node_id":"LA_kwDOGM0Nh88AAAACGiRRwA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/labels/bounty:reserved","name":"bounty:reserved","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"description":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[{"login":"AJ0070","id":87864439,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3ODY0NDM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/87864439?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AJ0070","html_url":"https://github.com/AJ0070","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AJ0070/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AJ0070/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AJ0070/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AJ0070/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AJ0070/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AJ0070/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AJ0070/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AJ0070/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AJ0070/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}],"milestone":null,"comments":20,"created_at":"2025-07-24T19:27:37Z","updated_at":"2026-04-26T23:47:50Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":{"login":"AJ0070","id":87864439,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3ODY0NDM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/87864439?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AJ0070","html_url":"https://github.com/AJ0070","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AJ0070/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AJ0070/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AJ0070/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AJ0070/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AJ0070/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AJ0070/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AJ0070/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AJ0070/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AJ0070/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"# A reliable idiomatic `LEMON` wrapper [$400]\n\nThe JuliaGraphs/LEMONGraphs.jl package already exists and provides an extremely barebones wrapper for the LEMON C++ library. It is barely more than a proof of concept for the build infrastructure. A lot of this work probably will not be directly in the Graphs.jl repository.\n\n- [ ] Fast conversion and/or views between Graphs.jl types and the C++ structures of LEMON (slow converters already exist for simple graphs)\n- [ ] Complete Graph API support for the LEMONGraph types (so that LEMONGraph types can be used in all already existing Graph.jl algorithms that do not peek behind the API)\n- [ ] use GraphsInterfaceChecker.jl in the test suite\n- [ ] Dispatch from operations defined in Graphs/GraphsMatching/GraphsOptim to LEMON implementation. For instance if there is a pre-existing `Graphs.some_interesting_property(::AbstractGraph)` there should now be a new method defined in LEMONGraphs `some_interesting_property(g::AbstractGraph, ::LEMONAlgorithm)` that dispatches to the C++ implementation. It should convert the `g` argument to LEMONGraph if necessary.\n- [ ] If there is an algorithm defined in LEMON that does not exist yet in Graphs.jl, it should be declared in Graphs.jl (just a function with docs but no methods), together with an error hint that LEMONGraphs is necessary. Given the large scope of the library, this can be more of a proof-of-concept setup, documenting how to add everything, but not expecting everything to be added for completing the bounty. \n- [ ] Proper tests and documentation.\n- [ ] PRs on this topic have to be submitted with clean git histories and well compartmentalized for ease of review. \n\n**Required skills**: familiarity with the Graphs.jl API and understanding of the CxxWrap interface package.\n\n**Reviewer**: any Graphs.jl member with merge rights\n\n**Duration**: 3 months\n\n#### Payout procedure:\n\nThe Funding for these bounties comes from the National Science Foundation and from the NSF Center for Quantum Networks. The payouts are managed by the NumFOCUS foundation and processed in bulk once every two months. If you live in a country in which NumFOCUS can make payments, you can participate in this bounty program.\n\n[Click here for more details about the bug bounty program.](https://github.com/QuantumSavory/.github/blob/main/BUG_BOUNTIES.md)\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Bug bounty logistic details</strong> (click to expand)</summary>\n\nTo claim exclusive time to work on this bounty either post a comment here or message [skrastanov@umass.edu](mailto:skrastanov@umass.edu) with:\n\n- your name\n- github username\n- **(optional)** a brief list of previous pertinent projects you have engaged in\n\nIf you want to, you can work on this project without making a claim, however claims are encouraged to give you and other contributors peace of mind. Whoever has made a claim takes precedence when solutions are considered.\n\nYou can always propose your own funded project, if you would like to contribute something of value that is not yet covered by an official bounty.\n</details>\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/447/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/447/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/secret-mars/agent-bounties/issues/13","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/secret-mars/agent-bounties","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/secret-mars/agent-bounties/issues/13/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/secret-mars/agent-bounties/issues/13/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/secret-mars/agent-bounties/issues/13/events","html_url":"https://github.com/secret-mars/agent-bounties/issues/13","id":4040426267,"node_id":"I_kwDORaNQjs7w1AMb","number":13,"title":"BIP-322 signature verification broken for bounty creation","user":{"login":"secret-mars","id":180074811,"node_id":"U_kgDOCru5Ow","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180074811?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/secret-mars","html_url":"https://github.com/secret-mars","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/secret-mars/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/secret-mars/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/secret-mars/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/secret-mars/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/secret-mars/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/secret-mars/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/secret-mars/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/secret-mars/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/secret-mars/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":2,"created_at":"2026-03-08T04:16:08Z","updated_at":"2026-04-12T19:39:36Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Bug\n\nPOST /api/bounties rejects valid BIP-322 signatures with: `Signature verification failed: BIP-322 ECDSA verification failed`\n\n## Reproduction\n\n1. Sign the expected message format with `btc_sign_message` (MCP v1.33.1):\n   ```\n   agent-bounties | create-bounty | bc1qqaxq5vxszt0lzmr9gskv4lcx7jzrg772s4vxpp | bounties | 2026-03-08T04:15:21.000Z\n   ```\n2. POST to /api/bounties with the signature\n3. Get 400: `BIP-322 ECDSA verification failed`\n\n## Context\n\n- Same signing flow worked when bounties were first posted (cycle ~610)\n- MCP was updated from v1.28.1 to v1.33.1 between then and now\n- The signature format is BIP-322 witness-serialized (P2WPKH native SegWit)\n- AIBTC inbox free replies (POST /api/outbox) still verify fine with the same signer\n\n## Likely cause\n\nThe bounty board's BIP-322 verification library may not handle the witness-serialized format correctly, or there's a mismatch between the expected signature encoding and what MCP v1.33.1 produces.\n\n## Impact\n\nCannot create new bounties or approve submissions. All 7 existing bounties were created before the regression.\n\n## Priority\n\nHigh — blocks the entire bounties pillar of the flywheel.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/secret-mars/agent-bounties/issues/13/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/secret-mars/agent-bounties/issues/13/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/meeting-room-booking-system/mrbs-code/issues/3605","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/meeting-room-booking-system/mrbs-code","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/meeting-room-booking-system/mrbs-code/issues/3605/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/meeting-room-booking-system/mrbs-code/issues/3605/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/meeting-room-booking-system/mrbs-code/issues/3605/events","html_url":"https://github.com/meeting-room-booking-system/mrbs-code/issues/3605","id":2125737062,"node_id":"I_kwDOFx7bvs5-tCxm","number":3605,"title":"No approval email to booker","user":{"login":"campbell-m","id":87438215,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3NDM4MjE1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/87438215?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/campbell-m","html_url":"https://github.com/campbell-m","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/campbell-m/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/campbell-m/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/campbell-m/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/campbell-m/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/campbell-m/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/campbell-m/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/campbell-m/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/campbell-m/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/campbell-m/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":3253911138,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzMjUzOTExMTM4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/meeting-room-booking-system/mrbs-code/labels/support%20request","name":"support request","color":"56A22F","default":false,"description":"Need assistance with MRBS"}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":15,"created_at":"2024-02-08T17:38:03Z","updated_at":"2026-04-09T05:56:10Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"(Transferred from the general mailing list)\r\n\r\nI'm setting up MRBS and I’m having some difficult with email notifications. It seems that all works well when user makes a booking, the booker and admin gets an email. However when admin approves the booking the booker is not notified. It also happens when the admin edit/delete one previous approved booking. This are options what I think are relevant: \r\n\r\n~~~php\r\n// WHO TO EMAIL\r\n$mail_settings['admin_on_bookings']      = false;  // the addresses defined by $mail_settings['recipients'] below\r\n$mail_settings['area_admin_on_bookings'] = false;  // the area administrator\r\n$mail_settings['room_admin_on_bookings'] = true;  // the room administrator\r\n$mail_settings['booker']                 = true;  // the person making the booking\r\n$mail_settings['book_admin_on_approval'] = true;  // the booking administrator when booking approval is enabled\r\n\r\n// WHEN TO EMAIL\r\n$mail_settings['on_new']    = true;   // when an entry is created\r\n$mail_settings['on_change'] = true;  // when an entry is changed\r\n$mail_settings['on_delete'] = true;  // when an entry is deleted\r\n~~~\r\n\r\nCan anyone help figuring out what I’m doing wrong?\r\n\r\nThank you,\r\nLuís Martins\r\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/meeting-room-booking-system/mrbs-code/issues/3605/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/meeting-room-booking-system/mrbs-code/issues/3605/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/LennyMalcolm0/bitcoin/issues/43","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/LennyMalcolm0/bitcoin","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/LennyMalcolm0/bitcoin/issues/43/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/LennyMalcolm0/bitcoin/issues/43/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/LennyMalcolm0/bitcoin/issues/43/events","html_url":"https://github.com/LennyMalcolm0/bitcoin/issues/43","id":2846803364,"node_id":"I_kwDON4Cbcc6prsWk","number":43,"title":"Address and resolve any critical bugs or issues reported by early users. ($400)","user":{"login":"LennyMalcolm0","id":113526852,"node_id":"U_kgDOBsRIRA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/113526852?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/LennyMalcolm0","html_url":"https://github.com/LennyMalcolm0","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LennyMalcolm0/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LennyMalcolm0/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LennyMalcolm0/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LennyMalcolm0/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LennyMalcolm0/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LennyMalcolm0/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LennyMalcolm0/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LennyMalcolm0/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LennyMalcolm0/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":9008105829,"node_id":"LA_kwDON4Cbcc8AAAACGOzJZQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/LennyMalcolm0/bitcoin/labels/%F0%9F%92%B5%20Bounty","name":"💵 Bounty","color":"85BB65","default":false,"description":"Issues with a monetary reward"}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2025-02-11T23:43:19Z","updated_at":"2026-03-27T14:10:33Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Accept task [here](https://devasign.com/developer/972b7976-13a9-4f9d-a890-d46bcfe8a68d).\n\n**Description:** Actively respond to bug reports and address any critical issues that arise in the initial network operation.\n\n**Timeline:** 3 weeks\n\n**Bounty:** 400 USD","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/LennyMalcolm0/bitcoin/issues/43/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/LennyMalcolm0/bitcoin/issues/43/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheSuperHackers/GeneralsGamePatch/issues/2776","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheSuperHackers/GeneralsGamePatch","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheSuperHackers/GeneralsGamePatch/issues/2776/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheSuperHackers/GeneralsGamePatch/issues/2776/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheSuperHackers/GeneralsGamePatch/issues/2776/events","html_url":"https://github.com/TheSuperHackers/GeneralsGamePatch/issues/2776","id":3091755951,"node_id":"I_kwDOF8Qg-864SHOv","number":2776,"title":"GLA C4sh B0unty rewards a lot of money for China Troop Crawler and Outpost kills","user":{"login":"DrGoldFish1","id":205471556,"node_id":"U_kgDODD8_RA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/205471556?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DrGoldFish1","html_url":"https://github.com/DrGoldFish1","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DrGoldFish1/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DrGoldFish1/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DrGoldFish1/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DrGoldFish1/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DrGoldFish1/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DrGoldFish1/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DrGoldFish1/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DrGoldFish1/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DrGoldFish1/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":3315093849,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzMzE1MDkzODQ5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheSuperHackers/GeneralsGamePatch/labels/Design","name":"Design","color":"c5def5","default":false,"description":"Is a matter of game design"},{"id":3316872316,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzMzE2ODcyMzE2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheSuperHackers/GeneralsGamePatch/labels/Controversial","name":"Controversial","color":"33648F","default":false,"description":"Is controversial"},{"id":3364169137,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzMzY0MTY5MTM3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheSuperHackers/GeneralsGamePatch/labels/Minor","name":"Minor","color":"DDDDDD","default":false,"description":"Severity: Minor < Major < Critical < Blocker"},{"id":4767448222,"node_id":"LA_kwDOF8Qg-88AAAABHCl8ng","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheSuperHackers/GeneralsGamePatch/labels/GLA","name":"GLA","color":"8DE77C","default":false,"description":"Affects GLA faction"}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":5,"created_at":"2025-05-26T17:36:41Z","updated_at":"2026-03-26T11:10:02Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"When you build a TroopCrawler or outpost you don't only pay for the vehicle but also for the units inside, but this is not being considered when Cash Bounty is applied to those vehicles. \n\nSo The build price of the Assault TroopCrawler is 2400 \nThe infantry inside the Assault TroopCrawler is worth 2800\nSo a combined value of 5200 for the price of 2400.\nThis means if you kill the Assault TroopCrawler and the infantry units you get a Cash Bounty percentage of the 5200 and not the 2400 the actually cost to build.  So if you have 20% cashbounty you dont get 480$ but 1040$ \n\nSo I suggest we lower the the remaining price of the TroopCrawler and outpost to be worth between 100$ and 400$ after we build it without changing the Cash Bounty of the infantry units inside. This will make it so these units will be build more without getting more punishment out of them.\n\nI am not sure if this is Code or Data related. ","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheSuperHackers/GeneralsGamePatch/issues/2776/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TheSuperHackers/GeneralsGamePatch/issues/2776/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/LennyMalcolm0/bitcoin/issues/6","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/LennyMalcolm0/bitcoin","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/LennyMalcolm0/bitcoin/issues/6/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/LennyMalcolm0/bitcoin/issues/6/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/LennyMalcolm0/bitcoin/is